  "result": "```json\n{\n    \"smpl.ordering.SimpleCORSFilter\": {\n        \"summary\": \"A Spring component that implements a servlet Filter to enable Cross-Origin Resource Sharing (CORS) for web applications. The filter intercepts all HTTP requests and adds CORS headers to the responses. Key methods: (1) doFilter() - the main filter method that sets Access-Control headers on the HTTP response including Allow-Origin (set to '*' allowing any domain), Allow-Methods (PUT, POST, GET, OPTIONS, DELETE), Max-Age (1 second), and Allow-Headers (Origin, X-Requested-With, Content-Type, Accept, Pragma, Cache-Control, If-Modified-Since), then passes the request through the filter chain; (2) init() - empty initialization method called when filter is instantiated; (3) destroy() - empty cleanup method called when filter is destroyed. This filter enables the application to accept cross-origin requests from web clients hosted on different domains, which is essential for modern web applications that may have their frontend and backend hosted separately.\",\n        \"file_path\": \"smpl/ordering/SimpleCORSFilter.java\"\n    }\n}\n```",
